    "field": "Planetary boundaries",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the absence of a quantified framework that defines a \"safe operating space,\" hindering humanity's ability to prevent its activities from pushing the Earth system beyond critical thresholds and causing unacceptable environmental change.",
    "method": "The authors propose identifying and quantifying nine planetary boundaries for critical Earth-system processes to define a safe operating space for humanity that, if respected, would prevent human activities from causing unacceptable environmental change.",
    "task": "The task is to identify and quantify a set of interlinked planetary boundaries for critical Earth-system processes that must not be transgressed to ensure a safe operating space for humanity and prevent unacceptable environmental change.",
